   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to classifying military\nmonuments and memorials as parkland",
    "basePrintNo": "S2328",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2328-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 42,
       "fullName": "James Skoufis",
       "imgName": "672_james_skoufis.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1232,
       "sessionMemberId": 2036,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "SKOUFIS"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §99-w, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2328\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to classifying\nmilitary monuments and memorials as parkland\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide statutory protection for veterans' memorials on public prop-\nerty throughout New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 2 of section 99-w of the general municipal\nlaw to require that military monuments or memorials under this section\nshall be considered as parkland in the municipality wherein such proper-\nty exists. Any change in status approved by the local entity under this\nsection shall not be alienated, developed, leased, transferred, sold or\ndiscontinued for use as a memorial site unless such action is authorized\nby an act of the legislature.\n\nSection 2 states that this law shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation designates veterans memorials on publicly owned proper-\nty as parkland and affords such property the protection of existing\nstate procedures related to the alienation of parkland when such changes\nare considered. Currently, there are not adequate protections in law to\nprotect veterans' memorials. This legislation will protect veterans'\nmemorials to ensure that the valuable purpose veterans memorials serve\nin our society will not be diminished.\n\nVeterans' monuments are deserving of additional protection. President\nFranklin Roosevelt held that view in 1933 when signed an executive order\nto bring historic battlefields and monuments under the control of the\nNational Park Service. Included was the Saratoga Battlefield in Stillwa-\nter.\n\nBy requiring the parkland alienation process for military monuments and\nmemorials we will be providing appropriate protection and oversight\nbefore changes in the status of these sites can be approved.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021/22: S242 (Mayer) / A7003 (Otis): referred to Local Government\n\n2019/20: S6677 (Mayer) / A8520 (Otis): referred to Rules; referred to\nLocal Government\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
